# 3. UI FINALIZATION — REMOVE ALL UNWANTED HOVER EFFECTS

This is a specific visual requirement.

Currently, some widgets change their appearance when the mouse pointer moves over them.

I do not want this behavior.

## A. Remove Widget-Level Hover Effects

Remove hover-triggered visual changes from every widget surface.

When the mouse enters a widget:

- Do not change the background color.
- Do not change the background opacity.
- Do not increase or decrease the widget scale.
- Do not move the widget.
- Do not alter its corner radius.
- Do not increase the shadow.
- Do not change border color.
- Do not introduce additional overlays.
- Do not reveal hidden toolbar elements.
- Do not reveal widget navigation tabs.
- Do not introduce unnecessary transitions.

The appearance of a widget must remain visually identical whether the mouse is outside or inside its area.

This applies globally to:

- Clock.
- Calendar.
- Weather.
- Pomodoro.
- Photo Frame.
- Agenda.
- Quick Actions.
- System Monitor.
- Notes.
- Todo List.

## B. Remove Hover-Revealed UI Elements

Some screenshots show small navigation tabs and additional labels appearing inside widget surfaces.

Remove these hover-triggered elements.

Do not expose debugging controls or widget management controls when the pointer enters a widget.

Widget management should remain accessible through an explicit configuration interface, Plasma widget settings, or a dedicated settings panel.

## C. Preserve Actual Interactions

Do not disable functional buttons.

Users must still be able to:

- Click buttons.
- Navigate calendar months.
- Start and pause timers.
- Open notes.
- Edit tasks.
- Navigate alarm slides.
- Open settings.

Keep keyboard focus indicators and accessible keyboard interaction.

Pressed or selected states may remain where necessary, but must not cause the entire widget surface to change appearance.

The default idle appearance must remain stable.

